{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a062e591bd4511cb7","tool_use_id":"toolu_0143vpnWKQ4LXwzLCnSsDWTM","description":"Implement warp-cooperative FRNN neighbor search kernel","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":false,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are implementing a performance-critical optimization to the FRNN library at /workspace/libFRNN/src/frnn.cu.\n\n## Context\n\nThe current warm GPU time for the real benchmark (271,663 points × D=12, radius=0.12, K=1000) is 307 ms. The goal is < 200 ms. The stage breakdown shows the neighbor search kernel (`stage_neighbor_search`) takes 304 ms — 99% of total time.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe current design processes one query per thread. With K=1000, the neighbor heap is in global memory. With 40,960 concurrent threads (40 SMs × 4 blocks × 256 threads), the active heap working set is:\n  40,960 threads × found≈34 × 8 bytes = 11 MB >> 4 MB L2 cache\n\nThis causes serial DRAM-latency chain: each heap insert depends on the previous result, and with L2 thrashing they go to DRAM (700 cycle latency). The heap does ~796 ops per query × 700 cycles = ~557,000 cycles per query of pure latency.\n\n## Solution\n\nSwitch from 1-thread-per-query to **warp-cooperative** (32 threads = 1 warp per query):\n- Distance computation parallelized: 32 threads handle 32 different candidates simultaneously  \n- Fewer concurrent queries: 40 SMs × 4 blocks × 8 warps = 1,280 active queries\n- Active heap working set: 1,280 × 272 bytes = 348 KB << 32 KB × 40 SMs = 1.28 MB L1 cache\n- Result: heap operations become L1 hits (4-20 cycles) instead of DRAM hits (700 cycles)\n\n## Implementation\n\nModify `/workspace/libFRNN/src/frnn.cu` to add a new warp-cooperative grid search kernel.\n\nKeep the existing `findNeighbors` kernel intact (it's still used for tests and correctness comparison). Add a new `findNeighborsWarpCoop` kernel and update the launch code.\n\nHere is the exact implementation to add:\n\n**New kernel** `findNeighborsWarpCoop` — insert this AFTER the existing `findNeighbors` function (around line 553 in the file), before the `launchBruteForceNeighbors` function:\n\n```cuda\ntemplate <int StaticDimension>\n__global__ void findNeighborsWarpCoop(\n    const float* query, int query_count,\n    const float* sorted_database,\n    const int* sorted_database_indices, int database_count, int dimension,\n    const GridParameters* parameters, const int* grid_offsets, float radius,\n    int max_neighbors, bool exclude_self, bool inputs_are_same,\n    const int* query_indices, float* neighbor_distances,\n    int* neighbor_indices) {\n  const float radius_squared = radius * radius;\n  const int lane = threadIdx.x & 31;\n  const int warp_in_block = threadIdx.x >> 5;\n  const int warps_per_block = blockDim.x >> 5;\n  const int work_index =\n      blockIdx.x * warps_per_block + warp_in_block;\n  if (work_index >= query_count) return;\n\n  const int query_index =\n      query_indices == nullptr ? work_index : query_indices[work_index];\n  const float* query_point = query + work_index * dimension;\n  float cached_query[StaticDimension == 0 ? 1 : StaticDimension];\n  if constexpr (StaticDimension != 0) {\n#pragma unroll\n    for (int axis = 0; axis < StaticDimension; ++axis) {\n      cached_query[axis] = query_point[axis];\n    }\n    query_point = cached_query;\n  }\n\n  float* distances =\n      neighbor_distances +\n      static_cast<std::int64_t>(query_index) * max_neighbors;\n  int* indices =\n      neighbor_indices +\n      static_cast<std::int64_t>(query_index) * max_neighbors;\n  int found = 0;\n  bool heap_mode = false;\n\n  int minimum_cell[kGridDimensions] = {0, 0, 0, 0};\n  int maximum_cell[kGridDimensions] = {0, 0, 0, 0};\n  for (int axis = 0; axis < parameters->grid_dimensions; ++axis) {\n    const float coordinate = query_point[axis];\n    minimum_cell[axis] = max(\n        0, static_cast<int>(floorf(\n               (coordinate - parameters->minimum[axis] - radius) *\n               parameters->inverse_cell_size)));\n    maximum_cell[axis] =\n        min(parameters->resolution[axis] - 1,\n            static_cast<int>(floorf(\n                (coordinate - parameters->minimum[axis] + radius) *\n                parameters->inverse_cell_size)));\n  }\n\n  for (int x = minimum_cell[0]; x <= maximum_cell[0]; ++x) {\n    for (int y = minimum_cell[1]; y <= maximum_cell[1]; ++y) {\n      for (int z = minimum_cell[2]; z <= maximum_cell[2]; ++z) {\n        for (int w = minimum_cell[3]; w <= maximum_cell[3]; ++w) {\n          const int cell =\n              ((x * parameters->resolution[1] + y) *\n                       parameters->resolution[2] +\n                   z) *\n                  parameters->resolution[3] +\n              w;\n          const int begin = grid_offsets[cell];\n          const int end =\n              cell + 1 < parameters->total_cells\n                  ? grid_offsets[cell + 1]\n                  : database_count;\n\n          for (int base = begin; base < end; base += 32) {\n            const int si = base + lane;\n            float cand_dist = radius_squared + 1.0f;\n            int cand_db_idx = -1;\n            bool cand_valid = false;\n\n            if (si < end) {\n              cand_db_idx = sorted_database_indices[si];\n              if (!(exclude_self && inputs_are_same &&\n                    cand_db_idx == query_index)) {\n                cand_dist = squaredDistance<StaticDimension>(\n                    sorted_database +\n                        static_cast<std::int64_t>(si) * dimension,\n                    query_point, dimension, radius_squared);\n                cand_valid = (cand_dist <= radius_squared);\n              }\n            }\n\n            const uint32_t ballot =\n                __ballot_sync(0xFFFFFFFFU, cand_valid);\n            uint32_t remaining = ballot;\n            while (remaining) {\n              const int src = __ffs(static_cast<int>(remaining)) - 1;\n              const float d =\n                  __shfl_sync(0xFFFFFFFFU, cand_dist, src);\n              const int db_idx =\n                  __shfl_sync(0xFFFFFFFFU, cand_db_idx, src);\n              if (lane == 0) {\n                selectNeighbor(d, db_idx, max_neighbors, found,\n                               heap_mode, distances, indices);\n              }\n              remaining &= remaining - 1;\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (lane == 0) {\n    if (heap_mode) {\n      sortNeighborHeap(distances, indices, found);\n    }\n    if (found < max_neighbors) {\n      indices[found] = -1;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**New launch helper** — add this after `launchGridNeighbors` (and its `#undef` at the end), right before the `countEdges` kernel:\n\n```cuda\nint blocksForWarp(std::int64_t query_count, int warps_per_block) {\n  if (query_count <= 0) return 1;\n  const std::int64_t blocks =\n      (query_count + warps_per_block - 1) / warps_per_block;\n  return static_cast<int>(std::min<std::int64_t>(blocks, 65535));\n}\n\nvoid launchGridNeighborsWarpCoop(\n    const float* query, int query_count, const float* sorted_database,\n    const int* sorted_database_indices, int database_count, int dimension,\n    const GridParameters* parameters, const int* grid_offsets, float radius,\n    int max_neighbors, bool exclude_self, bool inputs_are_same,\n    const int* query_indices, float* neighbor_distances,\n    int* neighbor_indices, cudaStream_t stream) {\n  constexpr int kWarpsPerBlock = 8;\n  constexpr int kThreadsWarp = kWarpsPerBlock * 32;\n  const int blocks = blocksForWarp(query_count, kWarpsPerBlock);\n#define FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(Dimension)                                   \\\n  findNeighborsWarpCoop<Dimension>                                         \\\n      <<<blocks, kThreadsWarp, 0, stream>>>(                               \\\n          query, query_count, sorted_database, sorted_database_indices,    \\\n          database_count, dimension, parameters, grid_offsets, radius,     \\\n          max_neighbors, exclude_self, inputs_are_same, query_indices,     \\\n          neighbor_distances, neighbor_indices)\n  switch (dimension) {\n    case 1:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(1);\n      break;\n    case 2:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(2);\n      break;\n    case 3:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(3);\n      break;\n    case 4:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(4);\n      break;\n    case 8:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(8);\n      break;\n    case 12:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(12);\n      break;\n    case 16:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(16);\n      break;\n    default:\n      FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP(0);\n      break;\n  }\n#undef FRNN_LAUNCH_GRID_WARP\n}\n```\n\n**Update `buildEdgesAsync`** — in the `buildEdgesAsync` function, find the `launchGridNeighbors(` call (around line 1026) and replace it with `launchGridNeighborsWarpCoop(`. The arguments are identical — just change the function name.\n\nThe exact text to replace is:\n```\n    launchGridNeighbors(\n        search_query, query_count, memory.sorted_database,\n        memory.sorted_database_indices, database_count, query.dimension,\n        memory.grid_parameters, memory.grid_offsets, radius, max_neighbors,\n        options.exclude_self, options.inputs_are_same,\n        search_query_indices, memory.neighbor_distances,\n        memory.neighbor_indices, stream);\n    checkCuda(cudaPeekAtLastError(), \"launch findNeighbors\");\n```\n\nReplace with:\n```\n    launchGridNeighborsWarpCoop(\n        search_query, query_count, memory.sorted_database,\n        memory.sorted_database_indices, database_count, query.dimension,\n        memory.grid_parameters, memory.grid_offsets, radius, max_neighbors,\n        options.exclude_self, options.inputs_are_same,\n        search_query_indices, memory.neighbor_distances,\n        memory.neighbor_indices, stream);\n    checkCuda(cudaPeekAtLastError(), \"launch findNeighborsWarpCoop\");\n```\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read the file `/workspa