orrectness tests: `ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure 2>&1`\n5. Run the real benchmark: `./build/frnn_benchmark --embedding data/embedding_data.csv --warmup 3 --iterations 10 --output /tmp/bench_warpcoop.csv 2>&1`\n6. Report the warm GPU p50 result from `/tmp/bench_warpcoop.csv` (look for `device_warm_gpu` row)\n\nDo NOT change the brute-force kernel. Do NOT modify the test file. Do NOT change the public API.\n\nThe `squaredDistance<StaticDimension>` function is already defined in the file and works correctly for the warp-cooperative case — all 32 lanes call it with different `sorted_database` pointer arguments (different candidate points), so each lane independently computes the distance for its candidate. The early exit `if (distance > limit) break;` causes SIMT predicated execution, which is correct.\n\nCritical correctness notes:\n- The `__ballot_sync` uses mask `0xFFFFFFFFU` (full warp)\n- The `__shfl_sync` uses mask `0xFFFFFFFFU` — all lanes participate even if some are inactive\n- The `while (remaining)` loop processes valid candidates one at a time\n- Only `lane == 0` calls `selectNeighbor` — other lanes are idle during this loop but the `__shfl_sync` calls still require ALL lanes to participate (hence the full mask)\n- The heap state (`found`, `heap_mode`, `distances`, `indices`) is only meaningful in lane 0\n\nReport back: whether tests pass, and the warm GPU p50 result."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0143vpnWKQ4LXwzLCnSsDWTM","session_id":"6f82439e-67c9-4df8-8006-0f75deb44a8f","uuid":"2d2fff61-2168-40f9-b96d-fa30ebffc747","timestamp":"2026-09-20T23:28:56.870Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement warp-cooperative FRNN neighbor search kernel"}
